From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valix <djvalic.wc@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] toolhead: do not log every SET_VELOCITY_LIMIT

Slicers send SET_VELOCITY_LIMIT ACCEL=... for each feature, and each call
logged a four-line block: 174k lines in one boot on one printer (issue
#40). Kiln OS: keep the values in the log rollover header (so each new
klippy.log still starts with the current limits) and keep the console
reply for a plain SET_VELOCITY_LIMIT, but stop writing every call to
klippy.log.
---
--- a/klippy/toolhead.py
+++ b/klippy/toolhead.py
@@ -583,7 +583,10 @@ class ToolHeadCommandHelper:
                "max_accel: %.6f\n"
                "minimum_cruise_ratio: %.6f\n"
                "square_corner_velocity: %.6f" % (mv, ma, mcr, scv))
-        self.printer.set_rollover_info("toolhead", "toolhead: %s" % (msg,))
+        # Kiln OS: slicers send this for every feature; keep it in the
+        # rollover header but out of the log (issue #40)
+        self.printer.set_rollover_info("toolhead", "toolhead: %s" % (msg,),
+                                       log=False)
         if (max_velocity is None and max_accel is None
             and square_corner_velocity is None and min_cruise_ratio is None):
             gcmd.respond_info(msg, log=False)
